        {
          "id": 414714276,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Actually ... since the value does need to be 16-bit in NBO prior to the hash input, isn't this approach safer if it is to work on both big- and little-endian machines? Maybe it'd be more clear to say `GUINT16_TO_BE((guint16)icmp_info->type)` instead.",
